From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: T8132: don't read a powered-down
 SIO in the gate check

Every T8132 deep sleep on the J604 so far has died in .enter's refusal
checks, on a read of the SIO's CPU control register (0x3ade00044): a
synchronous external abort, and with interrupts off the panic spun
until the watchdog. The SIO's entry in the gate list has no domain, so
its register is read whatever state SIO_CPU is in, and that domain is
not always-on: by then it is down. macOS on the J604 idles the SIO and
lowers SIO_CPU itself before the sleep, and doesn't touch the SIO
after that.

Give the SIO's entry its CPU domain, as the DCPs and the GPU have. And
read a gate's register only with its domain at full power, as the
unbound path already does, not at any nonzero state: below full power
the hardware has idled the domain, its registers may not answer, and a
CPU in it isn't running. macOS reads SIO_CPU at such a state (4) just
before it lowers it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 66b2da106b..44cc46bdd0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -1736,8 +1736,11 @@ static bool apple_sleep_gate_failed(struct apple_sleep *s)
 			}
 			continue;
 		}
-		/* A CPU whose domain is off isn't running, and its registers aren't there. */
-		if (g->ps && !sleep_ps_on(s, g->ps))
+		/*
+		 * A CPU whose domain is off, or idled below full power, isn't running, and its
+		 * registers may not answer: a read there is a synchronous external abort.
+		 */
+		if (g->ps && !sleep_ps_full(s, g->ps))
 			continue;
 		if (g->must_stop && (!g->asc ||
 				     ((readl(g->asc + ASC_CPU_CONTROL) & ASC_CPU_CONTROL_RUN) &&
@@ -4947,7 +4950,9 @@ static const struct apple_sleep_gate_coproc t8132_gate_coprocs[] = {
 	{ "/soc/dcp@30ae00000", true, 0x10000 },
 	{ "/soc/dcp@286e00000", true, 0x1e8 },
 	{ "/soc/dcp@48ae00000", true, 0x4f0 },
-	{ "/soc/pmp@380500000", true },	{ "/soc/dma-controller@3ade00000", true },
+	{ "/soc/pmp@380500000", true },
+	/* SIO_CPU, which its driver's runtime PM may power off: not always-on as the PMP's is. */
+	{ "/soc/dma-controller@3ade00000", true, 0x268 },
 	{ "/soc/nvme@40000" },		{ "/soc/mtp@394600000" },
 	{ "/soc/aop@390600000" },	{ "/soc/smc@38c600000" },
 	{ "/soc/sep@3aa600000" },
-- 
